; Stationery · Chronograph — the watch's materials in the Light look: a "panda" dial, a white plate with dark
; registers and a dark date window. Original work, MIT licensed. Theme-Dark.inc has the same names.
; The watch is an object: its plate, steel and register inks are its own, not the suite's ink.

[Variables]
; the glass shows only as the 8 pt crystal ring outside the plate
ChronoGlassTint=255,255,255,40
; the plate (a radial gradient, lit from above the centre); the second value of each is the solid plate (Cards: Solid,
; and the looks chosen by hand)
PlateCenter0=255,255,255,214
PlateCenter1=255,255,255,250
PlateEdge0=238,238,242,186
PlateEdge1=238,238,242,245
; the bevel on the plate's edge (light at the top), the minute track, the wordmark
CrystalTop=255,255,255,235
CrystalBottom=0,0,0,46
TrackMinor=0,0,0,110
TrackMajor=0,0,0,200
WordmarkInk=0,0,0,150
; batons, hands and cap; the 1 pt halo round the hands, the lume slot inside them
Hand=29,29,31,255
Halo=255,255,255,235
Lume=255,255,255,240
; the registers' faces, their snailing and steel rims, and the date window
RegFace=28,28,30,240
RegSnail=255,255,255,20
RimTop=250,250,252,255
RimBottom=142,142,147,255
DateFace=28,28,30,240
